## {{.StoreTitle}} and project

Slug, root and bound {{.Store}}: the session header `Project slug: ... Project root: ... Bound store: ...`. Header absent, or the user means another project (ask for its directory): run

```bash
"$HOME/.demarkus/bin/demarkus-plugin" registry project --dir <project-dir>
```

`<project-dir>`: {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}`"${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}"`, or the named directory as one POSIX-safe shell word{{else}}the absolute project directory as one POSIX-safe shell word; never wrap the raw path in literal single quotes{{end}}. Read its `verdict=` line: `use`: continue with `slug=`, `store=`, `root=`; `use, root unconfirmed: <reason>`: name the reason once, continue; `stop: <reason>`: relay it, stop, never fall back to the local {{.Store}}. A header marked stale or `Project: unknown` reads the same way. {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}Exit 127 (a sandbox, e.g. Cowork): Host-only commands stop; else the slug is the one the user names or confirms (`^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]*$`, never the working directory; ask once unless a blank slug means the whole {{.Store}}), the store `{{.MCPServerKey}}` (the local {{.Store}}), no more shell. Any other non-zero{{else}}Non-zero{{end}} exit, or a zero exit without a `verdict=` line: surface it, stop. `<root>` below is the project root: `/` for the {{.Store}}'s root project, else `/<slug>/`. Every `mark_*` call goes through the store's server{{if eq .Harness "claude"}} (`mcp__<store>__mark_*`){{else}} (the MCP server named `<store>`){{end}}; a tool not connected or missing (older binary): say so, name the server, point at `/soul-status`, stop.
